text.section:
Any pet shop that sells dogs shall maintain for each dog in its possession a written record that includes the following information:

The breed, age, and date of birth of the dog, if known;


The sex, color, and any identifying markings of the dog;


Any additional identifying information, including a tag, tattoo, collar number, or microchip;


Documentation of all inoculations, worming treatments, and other medical treatments, if known, including the date of the medical treatment, the diagnosis, and the name and title of the treatment provider;


For a dog obtained from a breeder or dealer, (i) the state in which the breeder and, if applicable, the dealer are located; (ii) the U.S. Department of Agriculture license number of the breeder and, if applicable, the dealer; (iii) the final inspection reports for the breeder and, if applicable, the dealer, issued by the U.S. Department of Agriculture from the two years immediately before the date the pet store received the dog; and (iv) the facility where the dog was born and the transporter or carrier of the dog, if any;


For a dog obtained from a public animal shelter, the name of the shelter; and


For a dog obtained from a private animal shelter or humane society, the name of the shelter or organization and the locality in which it is located.
